module Vt.View exposing (Shadow, shadow, frame, frameWith, frameBack, Highlight, noHighlight, inked, wantsFrame, Look, defaultLook, Focus, focused, Preedit, noPreedit, preeditSpot)

{-| The renderer's Geng side (`docs/phase2-window.md` §3, V18; in the
core's package by V19, `docs/renderer.md` §R6): a renderer that keeps its
own copy of the screen it drew and diffs the core's screen against it once
a frame, as PuTTY does.

The core's screen is one `Array.Builder` written in place, and a builder is
used once (geng-lang D963), so the renderer cannot keep last frame's handle.
It keeps instead:

  - `cells`, the cells it drew, `rows * cols`, `-1` where nothing is known;
  - `hashes`, a hash of each row it drew. A scroll is found by content: the
    longest band of rows whose hashes are the last frame's moved by `k`
    rows, up or down, with at least two rows in it that are not blank. The
    band is one `CopyArea`, and only what is left is diffed and drawn. The
    rows a scroll vacates keep their pixels, so the shadow keeps their
    cells. A false match costs a copy and is then drawn over: the diff is
    against what the pixels show, so it is never wrong.

The core's ring slots would say which rows moved without hashing, but the
core settles a region's turn by moving rows when the region changes, so a
slot is not a row's identity across a frame (§3).

A frame's display list is `Bytes`: first, in the first frame and in each
whose screen is not the size of the last one's, a size record (`0x04`, the
columns and rows in 2 bytes each), since the core may change its own size
(DECCOLM); then a style record for each style id
its runs use (`0x03`, the id in 2 bytes, then the foreground, background
and underline colours as RGB in 3 bytes each, the style's flags in a byte
as `Vt.Style.Attrs` has them, and its underline's kind in a byte), so that
whatever executes the list keeps no table between frames and resolves
nothing (`docs/renderer.md` V35); then a scroll record (`0x01`, top, bottom,
`k` as a signed 16 bits, rows `top + k` to `bottom + k` copied to `top`) and a run record per changed run (`0x02`, `y`, `x`, `n`, then each
cell: a byte of its width state in the top two bits (0 narrow, 1 the head
of a wide character, 2 its tail, 3 a spacer at a row's end) and its count
of code points below them, its style id in 2 bytes, and its code points in
3 bytes each: its cluster's, up to 63, §13). A run is a stretch of
changed cells, and never starts on a wide character's tail or ends on its
head. (Runs once took in gaps of fewer than four unchanged cells, so that
a glyph overhanging into its neighbour was redrawn with it, S§6.2; the
ink below does that, and a gap's cells, drawn again unasked, would fill
over ink it did not know to redraw.)

**Ink** (`docs/renderer.md` V40): a glyph is not clipped to its cells, and
an italic's hook, a Thai tone mark or a CJK glyph's top reaches into a
neighbouring cell. Whatever executes the list answers, for the cells it
drew, which edges each one's ink crossed, and [`inked`](#inked) keeps them
in the shadow. When a frame redraws a cell, it fills its background over
whatever ink lay there, so it redraws too every cell whose ink reaches
into it, and every cell whose ink reaches into one of those; and a cell
it redraws whose old ink reached its neighbours redraws them, since they
still show that ink. A scroll's
`CopyArea` copies the band's pixels and no more, so the cells at its edges
whose ink crossed them, and the cells next to it whose ink did, are drawn
again. While no cell has ink past its edges, none of this costs anything.

Ink overlaps: where two glyphs' ink meets, the one drawn later lies over the
other, and a screen drawn at once draws in reading order, row by row and
left to right. A glyph drawn new does not know its ink until it is drawn,
so when its ink reaches a later cell that holds a glyph and was not drawn
with it (to its right, or in the row below), that cell is forgotten and
[`wantsFrame`](#wantsFrame) asks for another frame at once, which draws
both in order. It costs a frame only where new ink lands on a glyph after
it.

**The cursor** is drawn as its cell's run, in a cursor style: the cell's
style id with its top bit set, `0x8000 + id`, whose record this frame
carries the cursor's colours and shape. The shape is the underline byte's
top four bits (1 a block, 2 an underline, 3 a bar, 4 a hollow block, which
is any cursor while the window does not have the focus, 5 none); its bottom four
are the underline's kind. A block's record has the cell's background as
its foreground and the cursor's colour (OSC 12, else the cell's
foreground) as its background; the others keep the cell's colours and
carry the cursor's as the underline colour, which whatever executes the
list draws the shape in. A wide character's two cells both take it. The
shadow keeps the cursor's cells marked (their shape in bits 56 and up, which
no cell of the core's has), so a cell the cursor leaves differs from what
the shadow says was drawn and is drawn again, and so is one whose cursor
changes shape. Nothing is drawn for a cursor DECTCEM hides. A blinking
one (mode 12) while `Focus.blinkOn` is false is shape 5, which draws
nothing and keeps the cell's colours: its cell is still the cursor's, so a
ligature stays broken there through the blink (`docs/renderer.md` §R19).
Blinking is the loop's, which knows the time.

A style's colours are resolved here, from the core's palette and dynamic
colours (OSC 4, 10, 11) and the profile's `Look`: inverse and the screen's
reverse video (mode 5) swap the two, faint takes the foreground half way
to the background, invisible makes it the background, and bold makes a
colour of the first eight its bright one when the look says so. A cell
whose style's colours change is not a changed cell, so when the palette,
the dynamic colours, mode 5 or the look change, the shadow is forgotten
and the frame draws every cell.

-}

import Array.Builder as Builder exposing (Builder)
import Bitwise
import Bytes exposing (Bytes)
import Int64
import UInt8
import Vt.Cell exposing (..)
import Vt.Term exposing (..)
import Vt.Screen exposing (..)
import Vt.Style exposing (Attrs, Clusters, Styles, cellPoints, styleOf)
import Vt.Palette exposing (programColour, paletteColour)
import Vt.Width as Width
import Dict


type alias Shadow =
    { cells : Builder Int64
    , hashes : Builder Int
    , cols : Int
    , rows : Int
    , frames : Int
    , scrolls : Int
    , moved : Int
    , drawn : Int
    , runs : Int
    , bytes : Int
    , colourKey : Int
    , stamps : Builder Int
    , styleIds : Builder Int
    , ink : Builder Int
    , inked : Bool
    , drawnIn : Builder Int
    , pending : Bool
    }


{-| What a profile says of colours: the default foreground and background,
which OSC 10 and 11 override, and whether bold brightens one of the first
eight palette colours. -}
type alias Look =
    { foreground : Int
    , background : Int
    , boldIsBright : Bool
    }


{-| What the window says of the cursor: whether the window has the focus,
and whether a blinking cursor is in the half of its blink that shows it. -}
type alias Focus =
    { focused : Bool
    , blinkOn : Bool
    }


focused : Focus
focused =
    { focused = True, blinkOn = True }


{-| What an IME is composing (`docs/phase3-input.md` V46): its text, each
code point's XIM feedback (reverse 1, underline 2, highlight 4), and the
caret, a count of code points. It is drawn over the screen from the
cursor, never written into it: each grapheme in the width the core gives
it, wrapping at the row's end, and past the screen's last row cut off. A
code point with no width joins the one before it, so Thai marks and
jamo stay with their base. The caret is the cursor while there is text.
Each feedback's style is one of the eight ids `Vt.Cell.styleMax` leaves
over: reverse video for reverse, bold for highlight, and an underline for
the rest, so plain composing text shows as composing. -}
type alias Preedit =
    { text : String
    , feedback : Array Int
    , caret : Int
    }


noPreedit : Preedit
noPreedit =
    { text = "", feedback = [], caret = 0 }


preeditStyle : Int
preeditStyle =
    32760


{-| A cell of the preedit's overlay: as the core's cell would be (its code
point, its width state, its style id in the high bits), and its code points. -}
type alias PreCell =
    { value : Int64, points : Array Int }


type alias Grapheme =
    { points : Array Int, feedback : Int, width : Int, caret : Bool }


{-| The preedit's graphemes: a code point with no width joins the one
before it; each takes its first code point's feedback and width, and
`caret` marks the one the caret is before. -}
graphemes : Preedit -> Array Grapheme
graphemes p =
    let
        cps =
            Array.map Char.toCode (String.toArray p.text)

        step i cp acc =
            let
                w =
                    if cp < 0x80 then
                        1

                    else
                        Width.width cp

                fb =
                    Maybe.withDefault 0 (Array.get i p.feedback)
            in
            when Array.last acc is
                Just g ->
                    if w == 0 then
                        Array.pushLast { g | points = Array.pushLast cp g.points } (Array.dropLast 1 acc)

                    else
                        Array.pushLast { points = [ cp ], feedback = fb, width = w, caret = i == p.caret } acc

                Nothing ->
                    Array.pushLast { points = [ cp ], feedback = fb, width = max 1 w, caret = i == p.caret } acc
    in
    Array.indexedMap (\i cp -> { i = i, cp = cp }) cps
        |> Array.foldl (\e acc -> step e.i e.cp acc) []


{-| The overlay's cells from the cursor, row by row; where the caret's
cell is (its index, and 2 for a wide grapheme); and where the reverse run
starts, else the caret. -}
type alias Overlay =
    { at : Int, cells : Array PreCell, caretAt : Int, caretCells : Int, spotAt : Int }


overlayOf : Preedit -> Term -> Overlay
overlayOf p t =
    let
        cols =
            t.cols

        start =
            t.y * cols + min t.x (cols - 1)

        limit =
            t.rows * cols

        place g acc =
            let
                i =
                    start + Array.length acc.cells

                col =
                    modBy cols i

                padded =
                    -- a wide grapheme that does not fit the row's last column
                    -- starts the next row, as the core's spacer does
                    if g.width == 2 && col == cols - 1 then
                        Array.pushLast { value = Int64.fromInt spacerHead, points = [] } acc.cells

                    else
                        acc.cells

                at =
                    start + Array.length padded

                id =
                    styleBits (preeditStyle + Bitwise.and 7 g.feedback)

                head =
                    { value = Bitwise.or id (Bitwise.or (Int64.fromInt (Bitwise.and 0x1FFFFF (pointsKey g.points))) (Int64.fromInt (if g.width == 2 then wideHead else 0))), points = g.points }

                cells =
                    if g.width == 2 then
                        padded |> Array.pushLast head |> Array.pushLast { value = Bitwise.or id (Int64.fromInt wideTail), points = [] }

                    else
                        Array.pushLast head padded
            in
            if at + g.width > limit then
                acc

            else
                { cells = cells
                , caretAt = if g.caret then at else acc.caretAt
                , caretCells = if g.caret then g.width else acc.caretCells
                , spotAt = if acc.spotAt < 0 && Bitwise.and 1 g.feedback /= 0 then at else acc.spotAt
                }

        placed =
            Array.foldl place { cells = [], caretAt = -1, caretCells = 1, spotAt = -1 } (graphemes p)

        caretAt =
            if placed.caretAt >= 0 then
                placed.caretAt

            else
                min (limit - 1) (start + Array.length placed.cells)
    in
    { at = start
    , cells = placed.cells
    , caretAt = caretAt
    , caretCells = placed.caretCells
    , spotAt = if placed.spotAt >= 0 then placed.spotAt else caretAt
    }


{-| A grapheme as a cell's low 21 bits: its code point, or for several a
hash with the cluster bit's place left clear, so the shadow sees a change. -}
pointsKey : Array Int -> Int
pointsKey points =
    when points is
        [ cp ] ->
            cp

        _ ->
            Bitwise.and 0x1FFFFF (Array.foldl (\cp h -> Bitwise.xor (h * 31) cp) 7 points)


{-| Where the IME's candidate window belongs, as a cell: the start of the
reverse run (the target clause), else the caret; the cursor's cell when
nothing is composed. -}
preeditSpot : Preedit -> Term -> { x : Int, y : Int }
preeditSpot p t =
    if p.text == "" then
        { x = t.x, y = t.y }

    else
        let
            o =
                overlayOf p t
        in
        { x = modBy t.cols o.spotAt, y = o.spotAt // t.cols }


{-| The core's palette's own: its white on its black. -}
defaultLook : Look
defaultLook =
    { foreground = 0xC5C8C6, background = 0x1D1F21, boldIsBright = False }


unknown : Int64
unknown =
    Int64.fromInt -1


shadow : Int -> Int -> Shadow
shadow cols rows =
    { cells = Builder.fromArray (Array.repeat (cols * rows) unknown)
    , hashes = Builder.fromArray (Array.repeat rows -1)
    , cols = cols
    , rows = rows
    , frames = 0
    , scrolls = 0
    , moved = 0
    , drawn = 0
    , runs = 0
    , bytes = 0
    , colourKey = -1
    , stamps = Builder.fromArray (Array.repeat 0x10000 -1)
    , styleIds = Builder.empty 64
    , ink = Builder.fromArray (Array.repeat (cols * rows) 0)
    , inked = False
    , drawnIn = Builder.fromArray (Array.repeat (cols * rows) -1)
    , pending = False
    }


{-| One frame: the shadow brought up to the term's screen, and the display
list that does the same to the window. -}
frame : Look -> Focus -> Term -> (taken sh0 : Shadow) -> { shadow : Shadow, list : Bytes }
frame look focus t sh0 =
    frameWith look focus noPreedit noHighlight t sh0


{-| The cells a selection covers on the screen drawn (`docs/phase3-select.md`
§14), `from` to `to` in reading order, both included, each `y * cols + x`;
`from` below 0 for none. A frame with one says so in a highlight record
(`0x05`, the first cell's row and column and the last's, 2 bytes each),
before its runs, and whatever executes the list draws each run's cells in
that range with their foreground and background swapped. The shadow keeps
a selected cell marked (bit 55), so a cell the selection takes or leaves is
drawn again. -}
type alias Highlight =
    { from : Int, to : Int }


noHighlight : Highlight
noHighlight =
    { from = -1, to = -1 }


{-| `frame`, with a preedit drawn over the screen from the cursor and a
selection highlighted. -}
frameWith : Look -> Focus -> Preedit -> Highlight -> Term -> (taken sh0 : Shadow) -> { shadow : Shadow, list : Bytes }
frameWith look focus preedit hl t sh0 =
    frameOn look focus preedit hl t.screen t.clusters 0 t sh0


{-| The frame of a view scrolled `back` rows up (`docs/phase3-select.md`
§11): `view` is `Vt.viewAt`'s screen of the rows it shows, drawn as the
screen is, so a scroll of the view is found and copied as output's is.
The cursor is drawn where its row has moved to, if it is still in view;
no preedit is drawn, since a key typed brings the view back down. -}
frameBack : Look -> Focus -> Int -> { screen : Screen, clusters : Clusters } -> Highlight -> Term -> (taken sh0 : Shadow) -> { shadow : Shadow, list : Bytes }
frameBack look focus back view hl t sh0 =
    frameOn look focus noPreedit hl view.screen view.clusters back t sh0


frameOn : Look -> Focus -> Preedit -> Highlight -> Screen -> Clusters -> Int -> Term -> (taken sh0 : Shadow) -> { shadow : Shadow, list : Bytes }
frameOn look focus preedit hl s clusters back t sh0 =
    let
        key =
            colourKey look t

        last =
            t.cols * t.rows - 1

        selFrom =
            max 0 hl.from

        selTo =
            min last hl.to

        cursor0 =
            cursorOf focus s back t

        plainCursor =
            if hl.from < 0 || selFrom > selTo then
                cursor0

            else
                { cursor0 | selFrom = selFrom, selTo = selTo }

        cursor =
            if preedit.text == "" || back /= 0 then
                plainCursor

            else
                let
                    o =
                        overlayOf preedit t
                in
                { plainCursor
                    | preAt = o.at
                    , pre = o.cells
                    , at = if plainCursor.at >= 0 || t.showCursor then o.caretAt else -1
                    , cells = o.caretCells
                    , shape = if plainCursor.shape == 0 then 1 else plainCursor.shape
                }

        sh1 =
            if t.cols /= sh0.cols || t.rows /= sh0.rows || key /= sh0.colourKey then
                let
                    fresh =
                        shadow t.cols t.rows
                in
                { fresh | frames = sh0.frames, scrolls = sh0.scrolls, moved = sh0.moved, drawn = sh0.drawn, runs = sh0.runs, bytes = sh0.bytes, colourKey = key }

            else
                { sh0 | styleIds = Builder.empty 64, pending = False }

        -- the shadow is made again at a change of size, so its rows are the
        -- screen's and its columns the term's
        rows =
            s.rows

        cols =
            t.cols

        current =
            Builder.toArray (hashRows s 0 rows cols (Builder.empty rows))

        band =
            searchK (1 - rows) rows current sh1.hashes { score = 1, top = 0, bottom = -1, k = 0 }

        scrolled =
            if band.bottom >= band.top then
                scrollBand band cols sh1

            else
                { shadow = sh1, list = Builder.empty 4096 }

        sh2 =
            spread s cursor rows cols scrolled.shadow

        diffed =
            diffRows s clusters cursor 0 rows cols sh2 scrolled.list

        sh3 =
            diffed.shadow

        ids =
            Builder.toArray sh3.styleIds

        styles =
            Array.foldl (styleRecord look t cursor.shape) (Builder.empty (14 * Array.length ids)) ids

        size =
            if sh0.frames == 0 || t.cols /= sh0.cols || t.rows /= sh0.rows then
                [ UInt8.fromInt 4 ] ++ Builder.toArray (push16 t.rows (push16 t.cols (Builder.empty 4)))

            else
                []

        highlight =
            if cursor.selFrom < 0 then
                []

            else
                [ UInt8.fromInt 5 ]
                    ++ Builder.toArray
                        (Builder.empty 8
                            |> push16 (cursor.selFrom // t.cols)
                            |> push16 (modBy t.cols cursor.selFrom)
                            |> push16 (cursor.selTo // t.cols)
                            |> push16 (modBy t.cols cursor.selTo)
                        )

        bytes =
            Bytes.fromUInt8s (size ++ Builder.toArray styles ++ highlight ++ Builder.toArray diffed.list)
    in
    { shadow = { sh3 | hashes = Builder.fromArray current, styleIds = Builder.empty 64, frames = sh3.frames + 1, bytes = sh3.bytes + Bytes.length bytes }
    , list = bytes
    }


{-| Each row's hash, pushed onto `acc`. A loop, because a function that
captures the screen to read it is refused: a capture takes the builder
(§3.3). -}
hashRows : (s : Screen) -> (y : Int where 0 - s.hist <= y) -> (rows : Int where rows <= s.rows) -> Int -> (taken acc : Builder Int) -> Builder Int
hashRows s y rows cols acc =
    if y >= rows then
        acc

    else
        hashRows s (y + 1) rows cols (Builder.pushLast (rowHash s (rowOffset s y) cols) acc)


{-| A hash of the row at `o`: its cells to its extent, and the extent. A
blank row's is 7. -}
rowHash : (s : Screen) -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> Int -> Int
rowHash s o cols =
    let
        ext =
            extentAt o s
    in
    Bitwise.xor ext (hashCells s o 0 ext 7)


hashCells : (s : Screen) -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> Int -> Int
hashCells s o x ext h =
    if x >= ext then
        h

    else
        let
            c =
                Maybe.withDefault 0 (Builder.get (o + x) s.cells)
        in
        hashCells s o (x + 1) ext (Bitwise.xor (rotl (Bitwise.xor (rotl h) (Int64.toIntWrap c))) (cellStyle c))


rotl : Int -> Int
rotl h =
    Bitwise.or (Bitwise.shiftLeftBy 5 h) (Bitwise.shiftRightZfBy 27 h)


type alias Band =
    { score : Int, top : Int, bottom : Int, k : Int }


{-| The best band over every shift `k` from `k` to `rows - 1`, 0 left out:
the one with the most rows that are not blank, more than `best.score`. -}
searchK : (k : Int where -1000 <= k) -> (rows : Int where rows <= 1000) -> Array Int -> Builder Int -> Band -> Band
searchK k rows current hashes best =
    if k >= rows then
        best

    else if k == 0 then
        searchK 1 rows current hashes best

    else
        searchK (k + 1) rows current hashes (scanY k (max 0 (0 - k)) (min rows (rows - k)) -1 0 current hashes best)


{-| Rows `y` to `end` at shift `k`: a run of rows that each match the row
`k` below it last frame, `start` its first row (`-1` outside a run) and
`score` its rows that are not blank. -}
scanY : (k : Int where -1000 <= k && k <= 1000) -> (y : Int where 0 <= y) -> (end : Int where end <= 1000) -> Int -> Int -> Array Int -> Builder Int -> Band -> Band
scanY k y end start score current hashes best =
    let
        closed =
            if start >= 0 && score > best.score then
                { score = score, top = start, bottom = y - 1, k = k }

            else
                best
    in
    if y >= end then
        closed

    else
        let
            h =
                Maybe.withDefault -2 (Array.get y current)
        in
        if h == Maybe.withDefault -3 (Builder.get (y + k) hashes) then
            scanY k (y + 1) end (if start < 0 then y else start) (if h == 7 then score else score + 1) current hashes best

        else
            scanY k (y + 1) end -1 0 current hashes closed


{-| The band moved in the shadow as one `CopyArea` moves it in the window;
with its ink, and with the cells at its edges whose ink the copy cut or
brought forgotten, so that they are drawn again. -}
scrollBand : Band -> Int -> (taken sh : Shadow) -> { shadow : Shadow, list : Builder UInt8 }
scrollBand band cols sh =
    let
        edges =
            if sh.inked then
                bandEdges band cols sh.rows 0 sh.ink []

            else
                []

        list =
            Builder.empty 4096
                |> Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt 1)
                |> push16 band.top
                |> push16 band.bottom
                |> push16 (Bitwise.and 0xFFFF band.k)
    in
    { shadow =
        { sh
            | cells = Array.foldl forget (Builder.copyWithin (band.top * cols) ((band.top + band.k) * cols) ((band.bottom + 1 + band.k) * cols) sh.cells) edges
            , ink =
                if sh.inked then
                    Builder.copyWithin (band.top * cols) ((band.top + band.k) * cols) ((band.bottom + 1 + band.k) * cols) sh.ink

                else
                    sh.ink
            , scrolls = sh.scrolls + 1
            , moved = sh.moved + (band.bottom + 1 - band.top)
        }
    , list = list
    }


-- WORDS


{-| A row's first index in the shadow's cells: `y * cols`, at most
999 * 1000, which the clamp says to the compiler, so that the sums after
it cannot wrap (`docs/vt-core.md` §VC58). -}
rowStart : (y : Int where 0 <= y && y < 1000) -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> (r : Int where 0 <= r && r <= 999000)
rowStart y cols =
    clamp 0 999000 (y * cols)


{-| Whether a cell is in a word: it has a glyph in what the core holds, or
in what was drawn there. A shaper chooses a glyph by its neighbours (a
ligature, a Devanagari conjunct, Fira Code's arrows) and shapes only the
cells a run gives it, so a cell is drawn with its whole word (see
[`spread`](#spread)). -}
inWord : (s : Screen) -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (y : Int where 0 <= y && y < 1000) -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x) -> Builder Int64 -> Bool
inWord s o ext y cols x cells =
    hasGlyph (cellOf s o ext x) || (x <= 1000 && hasGlyph (Maybe.withDefault unknown (Builder.get (rowStart y cols + x) cells)))


wordLeft : (s : Screen) -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (y : Int where 0 <= y && y < 1000) -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> Int -> Builder Int64 -> Int
wordLeft s o ext y cols x cells =
    if x > 0 && inWord s o ext y cols (x - 1) cells then
        wordLeft s o ext y cols (x - 1) cells

    else
        x


{-| Past the last cell of the word at `x`. -}
wordRight : (s : Screen) -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (y : Int where 0 <= y && y < 1000) -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x) -> Builder Int64 -> Int
wordRight s o ext y cols x cells =
    if x < cols - 1 && inWord s o ext y cols (x + 1) cells then
        wordRight s o ext y cols (x + 1) cells

    else
        x + 1


-- INK


{-| The ink of the cells a frame drew, as whatever drew it answers: for
each, its row and column in 2 bytes each, and in a byte the edges its ink
crossed (1 left, 2 right, 4 up, 8 down). A record off the screen is left
out. A cell after it in reading order that its ink reaches, that holds a
glyph and that this frame did not draw, is forgotten, and the shadow
wants another frame. -}
inked : Bytes -> (taken sh : Shadow) -> Shadow
inked answer sh =
    if Bytes.length answer < 5 then
        sh

    else
        let
            r =
                inkRecords answer 0 sh.cols sh.rows (sh.frames - 1) sh.drawnIn { ink = sh.ink, cells = sh.cells, pending = sh.pending }
        in
        { sh | ink = r.ink, cells = r.cells, pending = r.pending, inked = True }


type alias Inking =
    { ink : Builder Int, cells : Builder Int64, pending : Bool }


{-| `at` moved on `k` bytes in `b`, or to its end: never back, and never
past the end, so that the sum cannot wrap (`docs/vt-core.md` §VC58). -}
advance : Bytes -> (at : Int where 0 <= at) -> (k : Int where 0 <= k) -> (r : Int where 0 <= r)
advance b at k =
    if k < Bytes.length b - at then
        at + k

    else if Bytes.length b < at then
        at

    else
        Bytes.length b


inkRecords : Bytes -> (at : Int where 0 <= at) -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Builder Int -> (taken r : Inking) -> Inking
inkRecords b at cols rows stamp drawnIn r =
    let
        -- the bytes left from `at`: each read and the step to the next
        -- record are held to them, so that nothing wraps
        rest =
            Bytes.length b - at

        next =
            advance b at 5
    in
    if rest < 5 then
        r

    else
        let
            byte i =
                if i >= 0 && i < 5 && i < rest then
                    Maybe.withDefault 0 (Maybe.map UInt8.toInt (Bytes.get (at + i) b))

                else
                    0

            y =
                Bitwise.or (Bitwise.shiftLeftBy 8 (byte 0)) (byte 1)

            x =
                Bitwise.or (Bitwise.shiftLeftBy 8 (byte 2)) (byte 3)

            bits =
                byte 4
        in
        if y < rows && x < cols then
            inkRecords b
                next
                cols
                rows
                stamp
                drawnIn
                (Array.foldl (overlap rows cols (y * cols + x) bits stamp drawnIn)
                    { ink = Builder.set (y * cols + x) bits r.ink, cells = r.cells, pending = r.pending }
                    later
                )

        else
            inkRecords b next cols rows stamp drawnIn r


{-| The neighbours after a cell in reading order: to its right, and in the
row below. -}
later : Array Dir
later =
    [ { dx = 1, dy = 0, out = 2, back = 1 }
    , { dx = -1, dy = 1, out = 9, back = 6 }
    , { dx = 0, dy = 1, out = 8, back = 4 }
    , { dx = 1, dy = 1, out = 10, back = 5 }
    ]


{-| The neighbour of `i` in `d` forgotten if `i`'s ink reaches it, it holds
a glyph, and this frame did not draw it. -}
overlap : Int -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Builder Int -> Dir -> (taken r : Inking) -> Inking
overlap rows cols i bits stamp drawnIn d r =
    let
        n =
            neighbour rows cols i d
    in
    if n >= 0 && hasAll d.out bits && Builder.get n drawnIn /= Just stamp && hasGlyph (Maybe.withDefault unknown (Builder.get n r.cells)) then
        { r | cells = Builder.set n unknown r.cells, pending = True }

    else
        r


{-| Whether a drawn cell shows a glyph: a character past a space, a
cluster, or a wide character's tail, whose head draws one over it. -}
hasGlyph : Int64 -> Bool
hasGlyph c =
    c /= unknown && (cellPoint c > 0x20 || cellIsCluster c || cellWide c == wideTail)


{-| Whether a frame has been asked for at once: the last frame's ink
reached a glyph it did not draw (see the module's comment). -}
wantsFrame : Shadow -> Bool
wantsFrame sh =
    sh.pending


forget : Int -> (taken cells : Builder Int64) -> (r : Builder Int64 where Builder.length r == Builder.length cells)
forget i cells =
    Builder.set i unknown cells


inkAt : Int -> Builder Int -> Int
inkAt i ink =
    if i < 0 then
        0

    else
        Maybe.withDefault 0 (Builder.get i ink)


has : Int -> Int -> Bool
has bit bits =
    Bitwise.and bit bits /= 0


{-| The cells at a scroll's band's edges to draw again, read from the ink
before the copy: above the band, a cell whose ink went down into the band
or that the band's old top row's ink went up into; the band's new top
row, a cell whose own ink went up past it or below which the row above
its source had ink going down; and the same at the bottom. -}
bandEdges : Band -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Builder Int -> Array Int -> Array Int
bandEdges band cols rows x ink acc =
    if x >= cols then
        acc

    else
        let
            top =
                band.top

            bottom =
                band.bottom

            k =
                band.k

            above =
                (top - 1) * cols + x

            newTop =
                top * cols + x

            below =
                (bottom + 1) * cols + x

            newBottom =
                bottom * cols + x

            acc1 =
                if top > 0 && (has 8 (inkAt above ink) || vInto 4 ink cols (top * cols) x) then
                    Array.pushLast above acc

                else
                    acc

            acc2 =
                if has 4 (inkAt ((top + k) * cols + x) ink) || (top + k > 0 && vInto 8 ink cols ((top + k - 1) * cols) x) then
                    Array.pushLast newTop acc1

                else
                    acc1

            acc3 =
                if bottom + 1 < rows && (has 4 (inkAt below ink) || vInto 8 ink cols (bottom * cols) x) then
                    Array.pushLast below acc2

                else
                    acc2

            acc4 =
                if has 8 (inkAt ((bottom + k) * cols + x) ink) || (bottom + k + 1 < rows && vInto 4 ink cols ((bottom + k + 1) * cols) x) then
                    Array.pushLast newBottom acc3

                else
                    acc3
        in
        bandEdges band cols rows (x + 1) ink acc4


{-| Whether ink from the row starting at `row` crosses its edge `vbit` (4
up, 8 down) into column `x` of the next row: from the cell above or below
it, or from one beside that whose ink also crosses toward `x`. -}
vInto : Int -> Builder Int -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Bool
vInto vbit ink cols row x =
    has vbit (inkAt (row + x) ink)
        || (x > 0 && hasAll (vbit + 2) (inkAt (row + x - 1) ink))
        || (x < cols - 1 && hasAll (vbit + 1) (inkAt (row + x + 1) ink))


{-| What this frame draws, beyond the cells that changed: each changed
cell's word; every cell whose ink reaches into a cell drawn; every cell
the old ink of a cell drawn reached, which still shows it; and so on, the
cells forgotten in the shadow so that the diff draws them. -}
spread : (s : Screen) -> Cursor -> (rows : Int where rows <= s.rows) -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> (taken sh : Shadow) -> Shadow
spread s cursor rows cols sh =
    { sh | cells = spreadWork s rows cols sh.inked sh.ink (collect s cursor 0 rows cols { cells = sh.cells, work = [], worded = Builder.fromArray (Array.repeat (cols * rows) False) }) }


{-| The cells forgotten, the queue of those whose word and ink are still to
be followed, and the cells whose word is forgotten already: each word is
walked once, however many of its cells are queued, where walking it again
for each made a frame cost the square of a word's length (a row of 295
cells with no blank in it, as ConPTY writes them; puritty
`docs/windows.md` WS26). -}
type alias Work =
    { cells : Builder Int64, work : Array Int, worded : Builder Bool }


{-| Every changed cell, queued. -}
collect : (s : Screen) -> Cursor -> (y : Int where 0 <= y) -> (rows : Int where rows <= s.rows) -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> (taken w : Work) -> Work
collect s cursor y rows cols w =
    if y >= rows then
        w

    else
        let
            o =
                rowOffset s y
        in
        collect s cursor (y + 1) rows cols (collectRow s cursor o (extentAt o s) y 0 cols w)


collectRow : (s : Screen) -> Cursor -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (y : Int where 0 <= y && y < 1000) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x) -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> (taken w : Work) -> Work
collectRow s cursor o ext y x cols w =
    if x >= cols then
        w

    else if differs s cursor o ext y cols x w.cells then
        collectRow s cursor o ext y (x + 1) cols { w | work = Array.pushLast (y * cols + x) w.work }

    else
        collectRow s cursor o ext y (x + 1) cols w


differs : (s : Screen) -> Cursor -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (y : Int where 0 <= y && y < 1000) -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x && x <= 1000) -> Builder Int64 -> Bool
differs s cursor o ext y cols x cells =
    drawnAs s cursor o ext (rowStart y cols) x /= Maybe.withDefault unknown (Builder.get (rowStart y cols + x) cells)


{-| A neighbour of a cell: where it is, the edges a cell's ink crosses to
reach it (two of them for a corner, which the ink's box covers when it
crosses both), and the edges the neighbour's ink crosses to reach the
cell. -}
type alias Dir =
    { dx : Int, dy : Int, out : Int, back : Int }


dirs : Array Dir
dirs =
    [ { dx = -1, dy = 0, out = 1, back = 2 }
    , { dx = 1, dy = 0, out = 2, back = 1 }
    , { dx = 0, dy = -1, out = 4, back = 8 }
    , { dx = 0, dy = 1, out = 8, back = 4 }
    , { dx = -1, dy = -1, out = 5, back = 10 }
    , { dx = 1, dy = -1, out = 6, back = 9 }
    , { dx = -1, dy = 1, out = 9, back = 6 }
    , { dx = 1, dy = 1, out = 10, back = 5 }
    ]


{-| The neighbour of cell `i` in `d`, or -1 off the screen. -}
neighbour : Int -> Int -> Int -> Dir -> Int
neighbour rows cols i d =
    let
        x =
            modBy cols i + d.dx

        y =
            i // cols + d.dy
    in
    if x < 0 || x >= cols || y < 0 || y >= rows then
        -1

    else
        y * cols + x


hasAll : Int -> Int -> Bool
hasAll mask bits =
    Bitwise.and mask bits == mask


{-| The queue, a cell at a time: the cell forgotten, and with it its word
and the cells its ink and its neighbours' ink tie it to, each queued. -}
spreadWork : Screen -> Int -> (cols : Int where 1 <= cols && cols <= 1000) -> Bool -> Builder Int -> (taken w : Work) -> Builder Int64
spreadWork s rows cols inked0 ink w =
    when Array.last w.work is
        Nothing ->
            w.cells

        Just j ->
            let
                y =
                    j // cols
            in
            -- the queue holds only cells of the screen, which an array's
            -- elements cannot say
            if y < 0 || y >= s.rows then
                spreadWork s rows cols inked0 ink { w | work = Array.dropLast 1 w.work }

            else
                let
                    -- `modBy` by a width of at least 1 is 0 or more; the
                    -- `max` says so to the compiler (§VC57)
                    x =
                        max 0 (modBy cols j)

                    o =
                        rowOffset s y

                    ext =
                        extentAt o s

                    -- the word's ends, read before the cells are written;
                    -- none when its word is forgotten already
                    span =
                        if Builder.get j w.worded == Just True then
                            Nothing

                        else if inWord s o ext y cols x w.cells then
                            Just { l = wordLeft s o ext y cols x w.cells, r = wordRight s o ext y cols x w.cells }

                        else
                            Just { l = x, r = x + 1 }

                    popped =
                        { w | cells = Builder.set j unknown w.cells, work = Array.dropLast 1 w.work }

                    worded =
                        when span is
                            Just ends ->
                                forgetWord (y * cols + ends.l) (y * cols + ends.r) j popped

                            Nothing ->
                                popped
                in
                spreadWork s
                    rows
                    cols
                    inked0
                    ink
                    (if inked0 then
                        Array.foldl (pullDir rows cols ink j)
                            (Array.foldl (evictDir rows cols j (inkAt j ink)) worded dirs)
                            dirs

                     else
                        worded
                    )


{-| The cells from `i` to `end`, but `j`, forgotten and queued if not
forgotten already. -}
forgetWord : Int -> Int -> Int -> (taken w : Work) -> Work
forgetWord i end j w =
    if i >= end then
        w

    else
        let
            marked =
                evict i (i /= j) w
        in
        forgetWord (i + 1) end j { marked | worded = Builder.set i True marked.worded }


{-| The neighbour of `j` in `d` forgotten if its ink reaches `j`. -}
pullDir : Int -> Int -> Builder Int -> Int -> Dir -> (taken w : Work) -> Work
pullDir rows cols ink j d w =
    let
        n =
            neighbour rows cols j d
    in
    evict n (n >= 0 && hasAll d.back (inkAt n ink)) w


{-| The neighbour of `i` in `d` forgotten if `i`'s ink, `bits`, reaches it. -}
evictDir : Int -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Dir -> (taken w : Work) -> Work
evictDir rows cols i bits d w =
    let
        n =
            neighbour rows cols i d
    in
    evict n (n >= 0 && hasAll d.out bits) w


{-| The cell at `n` forgotten and queued if `there` and not forgotten
already. -}
evict : Int -> Bool -> (taken w : Work) -> Work
evict n there w =
    if there && Builder.get n w.cells /= Just unknown then
        { w | cells = Builder.set n unknown w.cells, work = Array.pushLast n w.work }

    else
        w


diffRows : (s : Screen) -> Clusters -> Cursor -> (y : Int where 0 <= y) -> (rows : Int where rows <= s.rows) -> (cols : Int where cols <= 1000) -> (taken sh : Shadow) -> (taken list : Builder UInt8) -> { shadow : Shadow, list : Builder UInt8 }
diffRows s clusters cursor y rows cols sh list =
    if y >= rows then
        { shadow = sh, list = list }

    else
        let
            o =
                rowOffset s y

            r =
                diffRow s clusters cursor o (extentAt o s) y 0 cols sh list

        in
        diffRows s clusters cursor (y + 1) rows cols r.shadow r.list


{-| The cell the core holds at column `x` of the row at `o`. -}
cellOf : (s : Screen) -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x) -> Int64
cellOf s o ext x =
    if x < ext then
        Maybe.withDefault 0 (Builder.get (o + x) s.cells)

    else
        0


{-| The cell drawn at column `x` of row `row` (the row's first index): the
preedit's where its overlay lies, else the core's. -}
cellAt : (s : Screen) -> Cursor -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (row : Int where 0 <= row && row <= 999000) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x && x <= 1000) -> Int64
cellAt s cursor o ext row x =
    let
        -- `preAt` 0 or more, so that the difference cannot wrap
        i =
            if cursor.preAt >= 0 then row + x - cursor.preAt else -1
    in
    if cursor.preAt >= 0 && i >= 0 && i < Array.length cursor.pre then
        Maybe.withDefault 0 (Maybe.map .value (Array.get i cursor.pre))

    else
        cellOf s o ext x


preCellPoints : Cursor -> Int -> Maybe (Array Int)
preCellPoints cursor i =
    if cursor.preAt >= 0 && i >= cursor.preAt && i < cursor.preAt + Array.length cursor.pre then
        Maybe.map .points (Array.get (i - cursor.preAt) cursor.pre)

    else
        Nothing


{-| Row `y` from column `x`: each changed run written to the list and the
shadow. -}
diffRow : (s : Screen) -> Clusters -> Cursor -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (y : Int where 0 <= y && y < 1000) -> (x0 : Int where 0 <= x0) -> (cols : Int where cols <= 1000) -> (taken sh : Shadow) -> (taken list : Builder UInt8) -> { shadow : Shadow, list : Builder UInt8 }
diffRow s clusters cursor o ext y x0 cols sh list =
    if x0 >= cols then
        { shadow = sh, list = list }

    else if drawnAs s cursor o ext (rowStart y cols) x0 == Maybe.withDefault unknown (Builder.get (rowStart y cols + x0) sh.cells) then
        diffRow s clusters cursor o ext y (x0 + 1) cols sh list

    else
        let
            x =
                if x0 > 0 && cellWide (cellAt s cursor o ext (rowStart y cols) x0) == wideTail then
                    x0 - 1

                else
                    x0

            end0 =
                runEnd s cursor o ext y (x0 + 1) x0 cols sh.cells

            end =
                if end0 < cols && cellWide (cellAt s cursor o ext (rowStart y cols) (end0 - 1)) == wideHead then
                    end0 + 1

                else
                    end0

            n =
                end - x

            written =
                writeRun s clusters cursor o ext (rowStart y cols) x end sh.frames sh.cells sh.stamps sh.styleIds (list |> Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt 2) |> push16 y |> push16 x |> push16 n)

            ink =
                if sh.inked then
                    clearInk (rowStart y cols + x) (rowStart y cols + end) sh.ink

                else
                    sh.ink
        in
        diffRow s clusters cursor o ext y end cols { sh | cells = written.cells, stamps = written.stamps, styleIds = written.styleIds, ink = ink, drawnIn = markDrawn (rowStart y cols + x) (rowStart y cols + end) sh.frames sh.drawnIn, drawn = sh.drawn + n, runs = sh.runs + 1 } written.list


{-| The cells a run draws, stamped with the frame. -}
markDrawn : Int -> Int -> Int -> (taken d : Builder Int) -> Builder Int
markDrawn i end stamp d =
    if i >= end then
        d

    else
        markDrawn (i + 1) end stamp (Builder.set i stamp d)


{-| The ink of cells about to be drawn forgotten: what draws them answers
it again. -}
clearInk : Int -> Int -> (taken ink : Builder Int) -> Builder Int
clearInk i end ink =
    if i >= end then
        ink

    else
        clearInk (i + 1) end (Builder.set i 0 ink)


{-| Past the last changed cell of a run that starts before `x`; `last` is
the last changed cell seen. -}
runEnd : (s : Screen) -> Cursor -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (y : Int where 0 <= y && y < 1000) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x && x <= cols) -> (last : Int where 0 <= last && last < x) -> (cols : Int where cols <= 1000) -> Builder Int64 -> (r : Int where last < r && r <= cols)
runEnd s cursor o ext y x last cols cells =
    if x >= cols || x - last > 1 then
        last + 1

    else if drawnAs s cursor o ext (rowStart y cols) x == Maybe.withDefault unknown (Builder.get (rowStart y cols + x) cells) then
        runEnd s cursor o ext y (x + 1) last cols cells

    else
        runEnd s cursor o ext y (x + 1) x cols cells


{-| The cells of a run, written to the list and the shadow; each style id
the first time this frame (`stamp`) is added to `styleIds`. -}
writeRun : (s : Screen) -> Clusters -> Cursor -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (row : Int where 0 <= row && row <= 999000) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x) -> (end : Int where end <= 1000) -> Int -> (taken cells : Builder Int64) -> (taken stamps : Builder Int) -> (taken styleIds : Builder Int) -> (taken list : Builder UInt8) -> { cells : Builder Int64, stamps : Builder Int, styleIds : Builder Int, list : Builder UInt8 }
writeRun s clusters cursor o ext row x end stamp cells stamps styleIds list =
    if x >= end then
        { cells = cells, stamps = stamps, styleIds = styleIds, list = list }

    else
        let
            c =
                cellAt s cursor o ext row x

            points =
                Array.takeFirst 63 (Maybe.withDefault (cellPoints c clusters) (preCellPoints cursor (row + x)))

            under =
                isCursor cursor (row + x)

            id =
                if under then
                    0x8000 + Bitwise.and 0x7FFF (cellStyle c)

                else
                    Bitwise.and 0x7FFF (cellStyle c)

            seen =
                Builder.get id stamps == Just stamp
        in
        writeRun s clusters cursor o ext row (x + 1) end stamp
            (Builder.set (row + x) (drawnAs s cursor o ext row x) cells)
            (if seen then stamps else Builder.set id stamp stamps)
            (if seen then styleIds else Builder.pushLast id styleIds)
            (Array.foldl push24
                (list
                    |> Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt (Bitwise.or (Bitwise.shiftRightZfBy 15 (cellWide c)) (Array.length points)))
                    |> push16 id
                )
                points
            )


push24 : Int -> (taken b : Builder UInt8) -> Builder UInt8
push24 v b =
    push16 (Bitwise.and 0xFFFF v) (Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt (Bitwise.shiftRightZfBy 16 v)) b)


push16 : Int -> (taken b : Builder UInt8) -> Builder UInt8
push16 v b =
    Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt (Bitwise.and 0xFF v)) (Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt (Bitwise.and 0xFF (Bitwise.shiftRightZfBy 8 v))) b)


-- COLOURS


{-| What a frame's colours are resolved from, as one number: when it
changes, every cell is drawn again. -}
colourKey : Look -> Term -> Int
colourKey look t =
    let
        mix h v =
            Bitwise.xor (rotl h) v
    in
    Dict.foldl (\k v h -> mix (mix h k) v)
        (mix (mix (mix (if Dict.get 5 t.modes == Just True then 1 else 0) look.foreground) look.background) (if look.boldIsBright then 1 else 0))
        t.colours


-- THE CURSOR


{-| Where the cursor is drawn, as an index into the shadow's cells (`-1`
for none), how many cells it covers, and its shape (1 a block, 2 an
underline, 3 a bar, 4 a hollow block, 5 none: a blinking one in the half that hides it). -}
type alias Cursor =
    { at : Int, cells : Int, shape : Int, preAt : Int, pre : Array PreCell, selFrom : Int, selTo : Int }


cursorOf : Focus -> Screen -> Int -> Term -> Cursor
cursorOf focus s back t =
    let
        blinking =
            Dict.get 12 t.modes == Just True
    in
    -- the cursor's row in the screen drawn is `back` rows lower in a view
    -- scrolled back, and is read only when it is in view
    if not t.showCursor || t.x >= t.cols || t.x < 0 || back >= s.rows - t.y || back < 0 - t.y then
        { at = -1, cells = 0, shape = 0, preAt = -1, pre = [], selFrom = -1, selTo = -1 }

    else
        let
            y =
                t.y + back

            o =
                rowOffset s y

            head =
                if t.x > 0 && cellWide (cellOf s o (extentAt o s) t.x) == wideTail then
                    t.x - 1

                else
                    t.x

            wide =
                cellWide (cellOf s o (extentAt o s) head) == wideHead && head + 1 < t.cols
        in
        { preAt = -1
        , pre = []
        , selFrom = -1
        , selTo = -1
        , at = y * t.cols + head
        , cells = if wide then 2 else 1
        , shape =
            if blinking && not focus.blinkOn then
                5

            else if not focus.focused then
                4

            else if t.cursorShape == 3 then
                2

            else if t.cursorShape == 5 then
                3

            else
                1
        }


isCursor : Cursor -> Int -> Bool
isCursor cursor i =
    cursor.at >= 0 && i >= cursor.at && i < cursor.at + cursor.cells


{-| The cell as the shadow keeps it once it is drawn: the core's, marked
with the cursor's shape where the cursor is. -}
drawnAs : (s : Screen) -> Cursor -> (o : Int where 0 <= o && o + s.stride <= Builder.length s.cells) -> (ext : Int where ext <= s.cols) -> (row : Int where 0 <= row && row <= 999000) -> (x : Int where 0 <= x && x <= 1000) -> Int64
drawnAs s cursor o ext row x =
    let
        c =
            cellAt s cursor o ext row x
    in
    let
        marked =
            if isSelected cursor (row + x) then
                Bitwise.or c (Bitwise.shiftLeftBy 55 1)

            else
                c
    in
    if isCursor cursor (row + x) then
        Bitwise.or marked (Bitwise.shiftLeftBy 56 (Int64.fromInt cursor.shape))

    else
        marked


isSelected : Cursor -> Int -> Bool
isSelected cursor i =
    cursor.selFrom >= 0 && i >= cursor.selFrom && i <= cursor.selTo


{-| A style id's record: its colours resolved (see the module's comment);
for an id of `0x8000` and more, its cell's under the cursor. -}
styleRecord : Look -> Term -> Int -> Int -> (taken b : Builder UInt8) -> Builder UInt8
styleRecord look t shape id b =
    let
        base =
            Bitwise.and 0x7FFF id

        a =
            if base >= preeditStyle then
                preeditAttrs (base - preeditStyle)

            else
                styleOf base t.styles

        cursorShape =
            if id >= 0x8000 then
                shape

            else
                0

        bold =
            Bitwise.and a.flags 1 /= 0

        fg0 =
            colourOf look t True bold a.fg

        bg0 =
            colourOf look t False False a.bg

        swapped =
            (Bitwise.and a.flags 16 /= 0) /= (Dict.get 5 t.modes == Just True)

        fg1 =
            if swapped then bg0 else fg0

        bg =
            if swapped then fg0 else bg0

        fg2 =
            if Bitwise.and a.flags 2 /= 0 then
                halfway fg1 bg

            else
                fg1

        fg =
            if Bitwise.and a.flags 32 /= 0 then
                bg

            else
                fg2

        ulc =
            if a.ulc == 0 then
                fg

            else
                colourOf look t True False a.ulc

        cursorColour =
            Maybe.withDefault fg (programColour 12 t)

        out =
            if cursorShape == 1 then
                { fg = bg, bg = cursorColour, ulc = bg }

            else if cursorShape == 5 then
                { fg = fg, bg = bg, ulc = ulc }

            else if cursorShape > 1 then
                { fg = fg, bg = bg, ulc = cursorColour }

            else
                { fg = fg, bg = bg, ulc = ulc }
    in
    b
        |> Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt 3)
        |> push16 id
        |> push24 out.fg
        |> push24 out.bg
        |> push24 out.ulc
        |> Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt (Bitwise.and a.flags 0xFF))
        |> Builder.pushLast (UInt8.fromInt (Bitwise.or (Bitwise.shiftLeftBy 4 cursorShape) a.ul))


{-| A preedit feedback's style: reverse video for reverse (1), bold for
highlight (4), and an underline otherwise. -}
preeditAttrs : Int -> Attrs
preeditAttrs fb =
    { fg = 0
    , bg = 0
    , ulc = 0
    , flags = (if Bitwise.and 1 fb /= 0 then 16 else 0) + (if Bitwise.and 4 fb /= 0 then 1 else 0)
    , ul = if Bitwise.and 1 fb /= 0 then 0 else 1
    }


{-| A colour of `Attrs` as RGB: 0 the default (OSC 10 or 11, else the
look's), 1 to 256 a palette index and one more, or `0x1000000` and RGB. -}
colourOf : Look -> Term -> Bool -> Bool -> Int -> Int
colourOf look t isFg bold c =
    if c == 0 then
        if isFg then
            Maybe.withDefault look.foreground (programColour 10 t)

        else
            Maybe.withDefault look.background (programColour 11 t)

    else if c <= 256 then
        let
            i =
                c - 1
        in
        paletteColour (if bold && look.boldIsBright && i < 8 then i + 8 else i) t

    else
        Bitwise.and c 0xFFFFFF


{-| Each channel half way from `a` to `b`. -}
halfway : Int -> Int -> Int
halfway a b =
    let
        channel shift =
            Bitwise.shiftLeftBy shift ((Bitwise.and 0xFF (Bitwise.shiftRightZfBy shift a) + Bitwise.and 0xFF (Bitwise.shiftRightZfBy shift b)) // 2)
    in
    Bitwise.or (channel 16) (Bitwise.or (channel 8) (channel 0))
